---
layout: base.njk
title: Methodology
isMethodology: true
---
<div class="section" style="padding-bottom:56px;max-width:800px;">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="section__intro" style="max-width:none;">
    Numbers on this site are computed deterministically from public data in Python and R. An AI
    assistant only turns already-computed figures into prose — it never calculates, estimates, or
    rounds a statistic itself.
  </p>

  <section style="margin-top:36px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:20px;">Why a town boundary, not a council boundary</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--text-muted);">
      {{ config.sources.council_transparency.council_name if config.sources.council_transparency else "The local council" }}
      is a large authority covering {{ config.locality.name }} and a lot of countryside and other
      towns in between. Filtering national data to the council alone would produce
      "{{ config.locality.region }}" content, not "{{ config.locality.name }}" content. Instead we
      use the Office for National Statistics' own settlement boundary — a Built-Up Area — which
      draws the actual edge of the town.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;max-width:420px;">
      <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:13px;padding:20px;background:var(--bg-elevated);">
        <span style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--text-muted);">REGION</span>
        <p style="margin-top:4px;font-weight:600;">{{ config.locality.region }} &amp; {{ config.locality.country }}</p>
        <div style="margin-top:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;background:var(--bg-sunken);">
          <span style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--text-muted);">LOCAL AUTHORITY</span>
          <p style="margin-top:4px;font-weight:600;">
            {{ config.sources.council_transparency.council_name if config.sources.council_transparency else config.locality.region }}
          </p>
          <div style="margin-top:12px;border:1px solid var(--accent);border-radius:8px;padding:12px;background:var(--accent-soft);">
            <span style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--accent-dark);">BUILT-UP AREA</span>
            <p style="margin-top:4px;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent-dark);">{{ config.locality.name }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text-muted);">
        What this site actually reports on: the innermost boundary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:36px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:20px;">Data sources</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-top:14px;">
      <table style="width:100%;font-size:13.5px;border-collapse:collapse;">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-muted);">Source</th>
            <th style="text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-muted);">Coverage</th>
            <th style="text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-muted);">Filtered by</th>
            <th style="text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text-muted);">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in methodologySources %}
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-weight:500;">{{ row.title }}</td>
            <td style="padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">{{ row.coverage }}</td>
            <td style="padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">{{ row.filteredBy }}</td>
            <td style="padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
              {% if row.isLive %}Live{% else %}<span style="color:var(--text-muted);">Coming soon</span>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% if row.isCommunityAreaJsna %}
          <tr>
            <td colspan="4" style="padding:2px 10px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
              <p style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text-muted);background:var(--bg-sunken);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;">
                <strong style="color:var(--text);">Boundary caveat:</strong> this source covers the
                {{ config.sources.community_area_jsna.area_display_name }} — Wiltshire's wider
                Community Area/Area Board geography (the town plus surrounding villages and
                parishes), not the Built-Up Area every other source on this page uses. Figures from
                this source should never be presented alongside BUA-based figures as if they
                describe the same population.
              </p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endif %}
          {% else %}
          <tr><td colspan="4" style="padding:14px 10px;">No sources configured yet.</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);">
      Generated from <code>config/{{ config.locality.slug }}.yml</code>'s sources block at build
      time — see the <a href="{{ '/data/' | url }}">Data hub</a> for fetch timestamps and download
      links per source.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:32px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:20px;">Every figure is traceable</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--text-muted);">
      Any number that reaches an article or a chart on this site carries its source URL and the
      timestamp it was fetched at. Nothing is published without that provenance attached.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:32px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:20px;">Human review, always</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--text-muted);">
      Scheduled jobs open a pull request when a new article is drafted; nothing goes live
      automatically. A person reads and approves every article before it publishes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:32px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:20px;">Licensing</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--text-muted);">
      All data used here is published under the Open Government Licence or an equivalent open
      licence, and this site's own output is offered under the same terms.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
